        "title": "Fuel Line Leak from Damaged Pump Retaining Tabs - NHTSA Recall 07V087",
        "description": "NHTSA campaign 07V087 covers certain 2001-2005 Saab 9-5 vehicles whose fuel-pump retaining tabs for the fuel-line connections may have been damaged during production. A connection can loosen and leak fuel, creating a fire risk in the presence of an ignition source. Applicability and completion are VIN-specific; the combined campaign population must not be presented as a 9-5 owner-report count.",
        "solution": "If fuel is smelled or seen, switch off the engine, avoid sparks or flames, move people away and arrange safe towing or emergency assistance. Check the VIN at NHTSA or with an authorized service provider. For an open campaign 07V087, the recall remedy is installation of the specified retaining bracket at no charge; do not improvise a clamp or disturb a leaking connection. Do not buy a fuel pump, line, seal or bracket from this page; recall completion and the exact remedy must be confirmed by VIN.",
