        "title": "V6 Ignition Discharge Module (IGBT) Overheating - NHTSA Recall 05V399/06V410",
        "description": "NHTSA campaigns 05V399 and 06V410 together cover specified 2001-2003 Saab 9-5 V6 vehicles with B308 gasoline engines. The campaign documents describe an ignition-discharge-module IGBT that can overheat and burn out, cause engine stall and increase crash risk; 06V410 expanded the V6 population. Applicability, campaign completion and the installed module version are VIN-specific and must not be inferred from symptoms alone.",
